  "query_preview": "..\n\n - Meteorological Overview:\n\nThis afternoon there is an upper-level ridge over North-central, \nCentral, and Southwestern Montana. This will bring dry and warm \ntemperatures (near seasonal averages) to the area on Wednesday.\nThis afternoon the pressure gradient increases which will bring \nbreezy conditions to the Rocky Mountain Front. On Thursday the \nupper-level ridge begins to break down. This will keep warmer \ntemperatures with mostly dry weather for the area on Thursday. \nThursday evening a cold front will move through North-central, \nCentral, and Southwestern Montana. \n\nOn Friday zonal flow is over North-central, Central, and \nSouthwestern Montana. This combined with the cold front that moved \nthrough will bring cooler temperatures (well-below seasonal \naverages). On Friday there will be rain showers across North-\ncentral, Central, and Southwestern Montana. On Saturday an upper-\nlevel ridge builds in briefly over North-central, Central, and \nSouthwestern Montana. This will briefly bring dry conditions to\nall but the Rocky Mountain Front and status quo temperatures to\nthe area. Sunday through Monday there will be upper-level closed \nlow that will bring cooler temperatures and widespread \nprecipitation to the area. Higher elevations locations have the \npotential to receive snow Friday through Sunday. See the Forecast \nConfidence & Scenarios Section for details. -IG\n\n - Forecast Confidence & Scenarios:\n\nOn Thursday there is greater than a 60% chance for wind gusts of\n45 mph or greater across the Rocky Mountain Front and Plains west\nof 1- 15, the Hi-Line, and Cascade to Judith Basin County. On \nThursday along the Rocky Mountain Front there is a 60 - 80% chance\nfor wind gusts of 55 mph or greater. \n\nSaturday through Sunday there is a 40 - 60% chance for 4 inches of \nsnow or greater along the Rocky Mountain Front. Saturday through \nSunday there is a 30 - 60% chance for 2 inches of snow or greater \nacross the Little Belts and mountains of Southwestern Montana. \nSunday morning there is a 20 - 40% chance for low temperatures of \n36 degrees or less across the plains of North-central Montana. On \nMonday there is a 60 - 80% chance for low temperatures of 36 \ndegrees or lower across the lower-elevations of North-central, \nCentral, and Southwestern Montana. On Monday there is a 30 - 50% \nchance for low temperatures of 34 degrees or lower across the \nlower-elevations of North-central, Central, and Southwestern \nMontana. \n\nOn Friday there is a 50 - 70% chance for a quarter inch of \nprecipitation across the majority of North-central Montana. On \nSaturday there is a 50% chance for a quarter inch of \nprecipitation or greater along the Rocky Mountain Front. On Sunday\nacross Central and North-central Montana there is a 50 - 70% \nchance for half an inch of rain or greater. On Sunday there is 30 \n- 60% chance for a quarter inch of rain or greater across \nSouthwestern Montana. -IG",
